Falsifies `system_tests::user::seventh_pass_retype_tests::a_grant_less_budget_narrows_a_split_child_and_every_retype_alike`.

Architecture: aarch64

The patch puts back, for one kernel object kind, the mint milestone 824 (a retype mints no right
its budget lacks) removed: `MemoryRegion::RETYPE_OBJ` hands back a rendezvous with `Rights::ALL`
whatever the budget holds. The frame step before it still holds, so the test fails at the first
object, which is the half the seventh outsider pass found the frame-only test did not reach.

Expected to fail: `assert_eq!` "a WRITE-only budget RETYPE_OBJ'd a rendezvous carrying more than
WRITE", with `left: Rights(31)` and `right: Rights(2)`. Replayed on 2026-10-12 (UTC) by milestone
824's lane: red at exactly that assertion on aarch64.

diff --git a/kernel/src/syscall/retype.rs b/kernel/src/syscall/retype.rs
index b72777aa3..ecc3be939 100644
--- a/kernel/src/syscall/retype.rs
+++ b/kernel/src/syscall/retype.rs
@@ -44,7 +44,7 @@ pub(super) fn memory_region_retype_obj(
             // could not narrow `deaths` to a right it did not itself hold, `CAP_INSERT` refused
             // the widen, and the spawn surfaced as `OutOfMemory` at a prompt. Inheriting from the
             // budget keeps that fixed, because the root budget is `Rights::ALL`.
-            let slot = sched::grant_from(floor, budget.mint_child(Object::Rendezvous(ep, 0)))
+            let slot = sched::grant_from(floor, crate::cap::rendezvous_cap(ep, Rights::ALL))
                 .map_err(|_| Error::OutOfMemory)?;
             Ok(slot as i64)
         }
